## 1. System Overview

{{ project_name }} is an Electric Power Steering (EPS) system providing
steering torque assist, position control, and return-to-center functionality.
Built on NXP {{ mcu }} with ASIL {{ asil_label }} safety integrity.

---

## 2. Torque Assist

### EPS-TRQ-001: Steering Torque Sensor
- The system SHALL read steering torque from two redundant TAS (Torque Angle Sensor) channels
- The system SHALL validate torque sensor signals by cross-checking both channels
- The system SHALL detect torque sensor failure when channel deviation > 10%
- The system SHALL use the lower torque value for assist calculation

### EPS-TRQ-002: Assist Torque Calculation
- The system SHALL calculate assist torque based on steering torque, vehicle speed, and steering angle
- The system SHALL apply a speed-dependent boost curve (more assist at low speed, less at high speed)
- The system SHALL update the assist torque setpoint every 1 ms
- The system SHALL rate-limit assist torque changes to 50 Nm/s

### EPS-TRQ-003: Motor Current Control
- The system SHALL control the EPS motor current via FOC (Field-Oriented Control)
- The system SHALL regulate motor current with ±1% accuracy
- The system SHALL detect motor overcurrent (> 100 A) within 100 µs

---

## 3. Position Control

### EPS-POS-001: Steering Angle Measurement
- The system SHALL measure steering wheel angle with ±1° accuracy
- The system SHALL determine steering direction and absolute position
- The system SHALL support angle range of ±720° (4 turns)

### EPS-POS-002: Return-to-Center
- The system SHALL provide return-to-center torque when driver releases the wheel
- The system SHALL adapt return speed based on vehicle velocity
- The system SHALL complete return-to-center within 2 seconds at low speed

---

## 4. Damping Control

### EPS-DMP-001: Active Damping
- The system SHALL apply active damping to suppress steering wheel oscillations
- The system SHALL adjust damping factor based on steering rate and vehicle speed
- The system SHALL prevent steering wheel wobble at high speeds

---

## 5. Safety Requirements (ASIL D)

### EPS-SAF-001: ASIL D Torque Monitoring
- The system SHALL implement two independent torque monitoring paths
- Path 1: Calculate max allowed assist based on lookup table
- Path 2: Monitor actual motor current and verify against allowed range
- The system SHALL disable assist on torque monitoring path mismatch

### EPS-SAF-002: Redundant Sensors
- The system SHALL use redundant steering torque sensors
- The system SHALL use redundant motor position sensors
- The system SHALL detect sensor faults within 1 ms

### EPS-SAF-003: Safe State
- The system SHALL disable motor assist on any safety violation
- The system SHALL maintain mechanical steering capability in safe state
- The system SHALL set DTC and notify driver via CAN

### EPS-SAF-004: Watchdog Supervision
- The system SHALL trigger watchdog at 10 ms interval
- The system SHALL monitor main control loop execution deadline
- The system SHALL enter safe state on watchdog timeout

---

## 6. Acceptance Scenarios

### Scenario: Normal Steering Assist
- GIVEN vehicle speed is 30 km/h
- WHEN driver applies 3 Nm steering torque
- THEN the system SHALL calculate assist torque within 1 ms
- AND the motor SHALL deliver the calculated assist within 2 ms
- AND measured assist torque SHALL be within 10% of demand

### Scenario: Torque Sensor Failure
- GIVEN TAS channel 1 reads 5 Nm and channel 2 reads 0 Nm
- WHEN deviation > 10% is detected
- THEN the system SHALL use the lower value (0 Nm) within 1 ms
- AND SHALL set a DTC for torque sensor plausibility
- AND SHALL disable assist within 10 ms

### Scenario: High-Speed Damping
- GIVEN vehicle speed > 100 km/h
- WHEN steering rate exceeds 100°/s
- THEN the system SHALL increase damping factor
- AND SHALL prevent steering oscillation

### Scenario: Safe State Activation
- GIVEN a safety monitoring mismatch
- WHEN the safety monitor detects torque path disagreement
- THEN the system SHALL disable motor assist within 2 ms
- AND SHALL notify the driver via CAN message
